NNAAMMEE
     ggggaatteell — GEOM Gate local control utility

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ggggaatteell ccrreeaattee [--vv] [--oo rroo | wwoo | rrww] [--ss _s_e_c_t_o_r_s_i_z_e] [--tt _t_i_m_e_o_u_t]
            [--uu _u_n_i_t] _p_a_t_h
     ggggaatteell ddeessttrrooyy [--ff] --uu _u_n_i_t
     ggggaatteell lliisstt [--vv] [--uu _u_n_i_t]
     ggggaatteell rreessccuuee [--vv] [--oo rroo | wwoo | rrww] --uu _u_n_i_t _p_a_t_h

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ggggaatteell utility is a local GEOM Gate class consumer.  It can be used
     as a replacement for md(4) devices or as a “GEOMificator” for non GEOM-
     aware devices, but it was mainly created as an example on how to use and
     how to communicate with the GEOM Gate kernel subsystem.

     Available commands:

     ccrreeaattee   Create a ggggaattee provider related to the given regular file or de‐
              vice.

     ddeessttrrooyy  Destroy the given ggggaattee provider.

     lliisstt     List ggggaattee providers.

     rreessccuuee   Take over a previously created provider and handle pending and
              future requests.  This is useful if the initial ggggaatteell process
              died.  To prevent data loss, the given path must lead to the
              regular file or device that was used to create the provider.

     Available options:

     --ff               Forcibly destroy ggggaattee provider (cancels all pending re‐
                      quests).

     --oo rroo | wwoo | rrww  Specify permissions to use when opening the file or de‐
                      vice: read-only (rroo), write-only (wwoo), or read-write
                      (rrww).  Default is rrww.

     --ss _s_e_c_t_o_r_s_i_z_e    Sector size for ggggaattee provider.  If not specified, it is
                      taken from the device, or set to 512 bytes for files.

     --tt _t_i_m_e_o_u_t       Number of seconds to wait before an I/O request will be
                      canceled.  0 means no timeout.  Default is 30.

     --uu _u_n_i_t          Unit number to use.

     --vv               Do not fork, run in foreground and print debug informa‐
                      tion on standard output.

     _p_a_t_h             Path to a regular file or device.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     Exit status is 0 on success, or 1 if the command fails.  To get details
     about the failure, ggggaatteell should be called with the --vv option.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     “GEOMify” the “fd0” device and use gbde(8) to encrypt data on a floppy
     disk.

           ggatel create -u 5 /dev/fd0
           gbde init /dev/ggate5
           gbde attach ggate5
           newfs /dev/ggate5.bde
           mount /dev/ggate5.bde /secret
           cp /private/foo /secret/
           umount /secret
           gbde detach ggate5
           ggatel destroy -u 5

